  "notes": "Net map (6 op-amp stages, all inputs traced at 12-16x). 0 = ground: GND 8/9/10/11/12/13 plus the non-inverting inputs of op-amps 2, 4, 5, 6, 7 and the bottom lead of vertical resistor 23. n1 = +15V node: V-DC(one port) 0, op-amp 2 in-, op-amp 2 out and the left lead of resistor 21 - the wire from the arrow runs right along y~148 to a solid junction dot at (26,148), and the rectangle (26,148)->(79,148)->(78,179) drops onto the output apex with a second solid dot at (78,179), so source, inverting input and output are one node. n2 = op-amp 2 output side of resistor 21 -> op-amp 3 in+ (T at (162,178) where the branch runs up to y~127) -> left lead of inductor 15. n3 = main distribution column at x~253 (longest net): inductor 15 right lead (top), op-amp 3 out (joins at y~185), left lead of resistor 25 (y~175), left lead of resistor 24 (y~264), and at the bottom the column turns right at y~372 into the left plate of capacitor 27. n4 = op-amp 3 in- : short left stub at y~198 then down x~173 to the node joining the right lead of resistor 22 (y~240) and the top of vertical resistor 23. n5 = +10V node: V-DC(one port) 1, T at (33,274) down to op-amp 6 in-, and left lead of inductor 14. n6 = op-amp 6 out -> right to the vertical at x~118, which also takes inductor 14's right lead (T at (118,276)) and runs up to y~240 into the left lead of resistor 22. n7 = resistor 25 right -> op-amp 4 in- , with the T at (318,171) branching up to y~138 into inductor 16's left lead. n8 = op-amp 4 out -> junction at (407,176) with inductor 16's right lead -> left lead of resistor 20. n9 = right-hand rail at x~506, continuous from y~173 to y~363: right leads of resistors 20, 18 and 19. n10 = resistor 24 right -> op-amp 5 in-, with the T at (323,262) running up to y~223 into capacitor 26's left plate. n11 = op-amp 5 out -> junction at (419,262) with capacitor 26's right plate -> left lead of resistor 18. n12 = capacitor 27 right plate -> op-amp 7 in-, with the T at (320,368) running up to y~328 into inductor 17's left lead. n13 = op-amp 7 out -> junction at (416,363) with inductor 17's right lead -> left lead of resistor 19. Judgment calls: (a) op-amp 2 really is drawn with its output strapped to the +15V node - both junction dots are unmistakable at 14x, so n1 carries four terminals even though it makes the stage a short; nothing was merged to make the validator happy. (b) Op-amp polarity read from the drawn +/- glyphs at 12-16x: op-amps 2, 4, 5, 6 and 7 all have '-' on the upper input and '+' on the lower; op-amp 3 is the only one drawn inverted ('+' upper, '-' lower), so its upper lead (from resistor 21/inductor 15) is in+ and its lower stub going down at x~173 is in-. Terminal order is (in+, in-, out) throughout. (c) The wire from the x~253 column into capacitor 27's left plate (y~372, x 259->293) is broken into faint dashes by JPEG compression, but the segments are collinear with the column's bottom corner and with the plate, and capacitor 27 would otherwise be a dangling terminal - read as a wire. Likewise the ~5 px gap between capacitor 27's right lead and the x~320 riser is a drafting gap, not a break. (d) Every op-amp here is drawn with a single feedback element (L15, L16, C26, L17, and the bare wire on op-amp 2) from output back to one input; that pattern was used as the sanity check on each T-junction. (e) All four inductors and both capacitors are drawn horizontally (leads left/right); resistor 23 is the only vertical passive, its lower lead going down to GND 10.",
